WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.040
Four crew.

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:01.760
One tank.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:02.640
Your command.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.400
Abrams Battle Tank by Dynamix

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.160
was a revolution for its time.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.520
Now, it's back!

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.360
Scan the horizon, work the terrain,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.240
and hold your crew together

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:11.760
when the shells start landing.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.240
Restored artwork.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.225
Reconstructed lettering.

00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:16.585
A choice of visual styles,

00:00:16.585 --> 00:00:18.265
including the one you first played.

00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:20.185
New sound effects and expressive crew voices

00:00:20.185 --> 00:00:21.545
bring every station to life.

00:00:21.545 --> 00:00:23.385
[Commander] T-72 destroyed.

00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:24.985
[Gunner] On the way!

00:00:25.305 --> 00:00:26.025
[Loader] Up!

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.025
[Driver] Engine is overheating

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:31.690
Underneath, the original
game still calls every hit,

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.770
every loss and every step of the campaign.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.250
On top, a tandem remaster in a new engine,

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.690
linked directly to the old one,

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.450
gives it a modern spit-shine.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.770
Save states mean one bad engagement

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.745
no longer costs you the whole campaign.

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:45.425
Fast-forward functions keep you engaged

00:00:45.425 --> 00:00:46.625
through the quiet parts.

00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:48.625
The remaster is free and open.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:50.945
Just bring your own copy
of the original PC game,

00:00:50.945 --> 00:00:51.665
then button up!

